// - Replaced `ARCHITECT_ROLES` object with a single `ARCHITECT_SYSTEM_PROMPT` that explains the Architect's identity, describes all 4 tools, when to use each, and the JSON schema for responses.
// - The player simply describes what they want in plain language. The AI decides which tool(s) to apply and tags each change with the tool used.
// - The input field is enabled immediately on open (no role selection required).
// - The diff card now shows `tools_used` at the top (e.g. "🔧 WORLDSMITH · LOREKEEPER").
// - The ledger records `tools` array instead of a single `role` string.
//
// 3. LANGUAGE-AWARE RESPONSES
// - `archSend()` injects the current story language (via `resolvePromptLanguage()`) into the prompt: "Respond in {language}. Your summary, warnings, and all text must be in {language}."
// - Adapts dynamically at runtime — if the story is set to Portuguese, the Architect responds in PT; English → EN; auto → follows context.
//
