// CHANGELOG - BergStoryChat v1.1.9.0 - 2026-07-24
// ============================================================================
//
// (CL18) PRISM FIX v4.1 — DOUBLE-FIRE, CANCELLATION & CONTEXT-AWARE SCORING - 2026-07-24
//
// CRITICAL FIX: Eliminated the triple-bug in the Prism suggestion system: double generation (wasting tokens), no cancellation of stale requests, and a mock scoring function that only measured text length.
//
// 1. DOUBLE-FIRE ELIMINATION (Bug #1)
// - `handlePrismPostSubmit()` no longer calls `triggerPrismGenerations()` on submit — it now only shows a waiting state, clears the defer timer, and aborts any in-flight generation. This was firing generation BEFORE the AI responded.
// - `window._prismOnProseEnd()` is now the SOLE trigger point: it fires exactly once, 400ms after the AI's prose finishes (when `state.turns` is updated), via a single `_prismDeferTimer` setTimeout. Previously both `handlePrismPostSubmit` AND `_prismOnProseEnd` called `triggerPrismGenerations`, causing 2 parallel generations = 6 expensive `ai()` calls.
//
// 2. CANCELLATION & ABORT INFRASTRUCTURE (Bug #2)
// - Added `clearPrismDefer()` and `abortPrismInflight()` utility functions that cancel pending defer timers and increment `currentPrismGenerationId` to invalidate all stale promises.
// - Added `_prismIsGenerating` lock to prevent concurrent generation cycles when `forceReload` is false.
// - Added `_prismAbortControllers` array to track AbortControllers for in-flight requests.
// - Both `handlePrismPostSubmit` and `_prismOnProseEnd` now call `clearPrismDefer()` before scheduling, preventing timer accumulation.
// - The old 800ms polling loop (up to 20 retries = 16s of wasted polling) replaced with a 1000ms defer (max 10 retries = 10s), using `clearPrismDefer()` to avoid stacking timers.
//
// 3. CONTEXT-AWARE CANON SCORING (Bug #3)
// - Rewrote `scoreCanon(text, tracker, ctxOverride)` to accept an optional context object and evaluate real narrative state instead of just measuring text length and trait-name matching.
// - New scoring rules: CRITICAL danger + combat keywords = +20, CRITICAL danger + social/flirt keywords = -30, HIGH danger + caution keywords = +15, NEGOTIATION + agreement keywords = +20, FLIRT + charm keywords = +20, INTIMIDATION + threat keywords = +15, low HP + short text = +15, low HP + aggressive keywords = -15, high tension + long text = -10, excessive exclamation marks = -15, very short text = -30, plagiarism of last turn text = -40.
// - Semantic tags from `SemanticEngine` now add +7 per partial match (first 5 chars) instead of +10 per full match.
// - Preserved the `currentTurnId` stale-abort check (returns 1 if turn changed during scoring).
//
// 4. UI LAYOUT — FULLSCREEN ON LOGO, ARCH REPOSITIONED, QUICK BG SELECTOR
// - Removed the fullscreen plugin button (`#Bfullscreen`) from the right sidebar header. Fullscreen toggle is now bound to the logo (`#Ebrand`) in the left sidebar header via click event, with dynamic tooltip updates on `fullscreenchange`.
// - Added `stopPropagation` on the theme selector (`#bergThemeSelect`) click to prevent it from triggering the logo's fullscreen toggle.
// - Repositioned the ARCH button to the left side of the right sidebar header (next to the panel toggle), with Gallery + Settings grouped on the right side separated by a flex spacer.
// - Added a compact background selector `<select id="bgQuickSelect">` between the ARCH button and the gallery button, listing all 24 backgrounds. Syncs bidirectionally with the existing `BACKGROUNDS` system and `applyBackground()`.
//
// ============================================================================
